cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RAVEL: agent-driven reinterpretation of LHC searches"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the foundational tools listed under references."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ammar
    family-names: Aziz
abstract: >-
  RAVEL reinterprets published ATLAS and CMS searches. A coding agent plans each calculation and
  stops for the physicist's approval at check-ins; the ravel package runs and checks
  MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, Pythia 8, Delphes with SimpleAnalysis or Rivet, and pyhf, and reports a 95%
  CLs exclusion limit with the evidence behind it. Likelihood-only and generation-only runs and
  studies of supplied events or models are also supported. Validation records distinguish
  statistical S95 recovery, selection acceptance and efficiency, and end-to-end mass-plane
  fidelity. Failed and unscorable cases are retained.
keywords:
  - high-energy physics
  - LHC reinterpretation
  - recasting
  - supersymmetry
  - agentic workflow
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ammarphp/ravel"
version: 0.4.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Reduce, Reuse, Reinterpret: an end-to-end pipeline for recycling particle physics results"
    authors:
      - family-names: Stark
        given-names: Giordon
      - family-names: Aristimuno Ots
        given-names: Camila
      - family-names: Hance
        given-names: Mike
    notes: "the mapyde package; arXiv:2306.11055; SciPost Phys. Codebases 27 (2024)"
  - type: software
    title: "Rivet"
    notes: "particle-level analysis framework"
  - type: software
    title: "pyhf"
    notes: "pure-Python HistFactory; public ATLAS likelihoods"
  - type: software
    title: "SModelS"
  - type: software
    title: "MadAnalysis 5"
